<title>SWITZERLAND: Baer takes stake in Swiss private bank.</title>
<headline>Baer takes stake in Swiss private bank.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portfolio manager Julius Baer Holding AG said it had taken a 51 percent stake in a new Swiss private bank being founded in the central Swiss city of Lucerne with private asset managers Falck &amp; Cie.</p>
<p>A Baer statement said the new company, Bank Falck &amp; Co AG, would assume the active business operations of Falck &amp; Cie, founded in 1875 and the only private bank group based in central Switzerland. Falck has 30 employees.</p>
<p>The nominal share capital of Bank Falck will total 10 million Swiss francs. Falck &amp; Cie will hold 49 percent.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
